    addEvent: 'Alan Kay conceives the Dynabook concept, laying the theoretical groundwork for object-oriented user interfaces.' on: '1972.1.1';
    addEvent: 'Smalltalk-72 is developed at Xerox PARC, functioning as the first live, dynamic programming environment.' on: '1972.7.1';
    addEvent: 'Smalltalk-76 introduces class-based inheritance, metaclasses, and the iconic overlapping windows GUI.' on: '1976.1.1';
    addEvent: 'Smalltalk-80 is released to the public, establishing the standard language specification and MVC pattern.' on: '1980.1.1';
    addEvent: 'Digitalk launches Smalltalk/V, bringing affordable object-oriented programming to IBM PCs.' on: '1986.1.1';
    addEvent: 'ParcPlace Systems is spun off from Xerox PARC to commercialize Smalltalk-80 for workstations.' on: '1988.1.1';
    addEvent: 'ObjectShare releases VisualWorks, unifying commercial Smalltalk development across platforms.' on: '1992.1.1';
    addEvent: 'Squeak is released as an open-source, highly portable implementation of Smalltalk-80 by original pioneers.' on: '1996.3.1';
    addEvent: 'Pharo begins as an open-source fork of Squeak, focused on cleaning up and modernizing the environment.' on: '2008.1.1';
    addEvent: 'Cuis-Smalltalk is established as a lean, elegant, and inspectable modern derivative of Smalltalk-80.' on: '2008.9.1';
